<%# locals: (ps:) %>

<div>
  <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold leading-7 text-gray-900 sm:truncate sm:text-2xl sm:tracking-tight">
    VPC Peering
  </h3>

  <p class="text-gray-500 mt-2">
    Connect this subnet's VPC network to a VPC network in your own GCP project so your applications reach it over
    private addresses. Ubicloud adds its side of the peering; you create the matching side in your project.
  </p>
</div>

<%== part(
  "components/kv_data_card",
  data: [
    ["Ubicloud project", ps.location.location_credential_gcp.project_id, {copyable: true}],
    ["Ubicloud VPC network", ps.gcp_vpc.name, {copyable: true}],
    ["CIDR", ps.net4.to_s, {copyable: true}]
  ]
) %>

<p class="text-sm text-gray-500">
  No subnet range of your network may overlap <%= ps.net4.to_s %>, the imported subnet routes of this subnet's other
  peerings (listed below), or the subnets of any network peered with yours. GCP exchanges only private IPv4 subnet
  routes: no custom routes, no IPv6 and no transit through other peerings. Only private subnets with their own VPC
  network can be peered, and each one needs its own peering, so this peering does not reach your other private subnets
  or PostgreSQL databases.
</p>

<p class="text-sm text-gray-500">
  Connections can be opened only from your network into this subnet. Machines in this subnet cannot open connections to
  your network.
</p>
